{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.QuantumGLCommutant","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.QuantumGLCommutant","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.QuantumGLWeights","lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.QuantumGLHWBound","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.BilinearForm.Orthogonal","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.DotProduct","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.FreeModule.Finite.Matrix"],"declarations":38,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.QuantumGL.range_jimbo_eq_commutant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.QuantumGL.range_jimbo_eq_commutant","kind":"theorem","line":415,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/QuantumGLCommutant.lean#L415-L425","doc":"**G3.4**: over a linearly ordered field and for `q` not a root of unity, the image of\n`H_{m+1}(q)` under the `gl_d` Jimbo action is exactly the commutant of the operators in `uqGens`:\n`E_i = raiseOp`, `lowerOp`, the Cartan elements and the weight projectors on `(L^d)^{⊗(m+1)}`.\nScope: this is not yet the commutant of `U_q(gl_d)` itself. That needs (1) the weight projectors to\nbe polynomials in the Cartan elements at generic `q`, and (2) `lowerOp` and the standard `Δ(F)` to\ngenerate the same algebra with the Cartan elements. Both are open (bean `qou-gl34`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.QuantumGL.sub_inv_ne_zero_of_notRootOfUnity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.QuantumGL.sub_inv_ne_zero_of_notRootOfUnity","kind":"theorem","line":406,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/QuantumGLCommutant.lean#L406-L413","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.QuantumGL.range_jimbo_eq_commutant_of_hstar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.QuantumGL.range_jimbo_eq_commutant_of_hstar","kind":"theorem","line":390,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/QuantumGLCommutant.lean#L390-L404","doc":"**G3.4 from (★)**: the Jimbo image is the full commutant, given the bound (★) as the\nhypothesis `hstar`. `range_jimbo_eq_commutant` discharges it with `hstar_occWeights`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.QuantumGL.finrank_commutant_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.QuantumGL.finrank_commutant_le","kind":"theorem","line":377,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/QuantumGLCommutant.lean#L377-L386","doc":"**F3: `dim B' ≤ Σ_μ (dim N_μ)²`.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.QuantumGL.resHW_injective","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.QuantumGL.resHW_injective","kind":"theorem","line":355,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/QuantumGLCommutant.lean#L355-L375","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.QuantumGL.resHW","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.QuantumGL.resHW","kind":"def","line":343,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/QuantumGLCommutant.lean#L343-L353","doc":"Restriction of a commutant element to the highest-weight spaces. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.QuantumGL.mulVec_mem_hwSpace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.QuantumGL.mulVec_mem_hwSpace","kind":"theorem","line":335,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/QuantumGLCommutant.lean#L335-L341","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.S